text:
alex: Quick design check — inline errors vs top summary on the new 'Create Pipeline' form. Attached screenshot: https://figma.redwood/mock. My gut: inline for field-level issues, summary toast for batch/submission failures. Thoughts?

priya: +1 for inline. For accessibility we need aria-live on the inline error region so screen readers announce changes. Also prefer explicit field names in the message.

marco: Agree. Also we should standardize how we show required: asterisk alone is ambiguous. Suggest a small subdued asterisk plus visible label for first-run flows. :thinking_face: 

jen: Concern about visual noise if we add "Required" everywhere. Could we use an asterisk visually and add a screen-reader-only "required" string for accessibility? Example CSS we use:```css
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0,0,0,0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
}
```

alex: Good call — a11y-first but keep a visible cue. Proposal: subdued asterisk (contrast tested) + sr-only "required". :+1:

priya: Also microcopy: error messages should include the field label. e.g., instead of "Invalid input" prefer "Email — enter a valid email address." Copy variants:```
- Email — enter a valid email address
- Name — please include first and last name
```

sam: On destructive confirms: delete pipeline modal — debate between typed-confirm vs checkbox confirm. Ops likes typed-confirm for safety. UX worried about friction for common dev flows.

marco: What about conditional typed-confirm? Require typed-confirm for pipelines with a "production" tag or >100 users; otherwise show checkbox + bold warning.

jen: Also check dialog semantics: use role="alertdialog" for the confirm modal and link aria-describedby to the explanatory text. Ensure focus trap and return focus to the delete button on cancel.

a11y-bot: Accessibility note: use aria-live="polite" or "assertive" depending on severity for inline errors, set aria-atomic="true" for consistent announcements. Ensure asterisk color contrast >= 4.5:1.

alex: I'll update Figma with three variants (asterisk+sr-only, visible "Required" on hover, and persistent label) and a prototype for keyboard-only and screenreader flows.

priya: Can we add E2E test cases too: screenreader reads inline error on submit, typed-confirm requires exact phrase, cancel returns focus, and error link focuses the first errored input.

sam: I'll add telemetry: confirm_type (typed|checkbox|none), and a post-delete incident checklist for accidental deletes. Will own rollout guardrails.

alex: Action items: alex -> update Figma + prototype; priya -> finalize microcopy + a11y test matrix; sam -> telemetry + incident playbook; jen -> modal accessibility checklist. I'll loop in PM for rollout cadence.

marco: Looks good. One last nit: ensure the inline error link uses an accessible name like "Fix email input" not "Click here".

jen: Agreed. Small copy tweak then we can ship the pattern doc.

alex: Thanks all — will push mocks by EOD and ping for quick UX review. :rocket:
